>>That's just my situation. I often "hear" sounds, like someone's
>>counting money and a shopowner cursing shoplifters - so I want to
>>search for a hidden door to the shop.
> Heres some tips on picking where to search:
>   1) Passage ways that just suddenly end are suspicious, try search at
>      the end of them, then working back searching as you go.

I seem to find a lot more "genuine" dead-end passages in 3.4.3, though 
that could just be me.

>   2) Remember that the map is limited to the screen- if you are in a
>      room on the far right side of the screen, you are less likely to
>      find a door (leading anywhere new) on the right than on the left. 

Less likely, but not completely unlikely. Do search in the areas near 
map centre first, but don't discount the possibility.

>   3) Shops are usually (but not always) near the edge of the screen-

(because the shop is randomly generated in a room with only 1 door, IIRC)

>      they also need some space, so look for regions of the map
>      you havent found anything in yet.

True not just for shops. If there's a big empty region, chances are 
there's something hidden there (not always!)

> You could also use magical means to figure out what the whole level looks
> like, find the secret doors nearby, figure out where the shop is, or maybe
> even other things..

Or you could bypass it and come back later. There are some items which 
allow you to make your own path through the level; using these is 
sometimes faster than searching.

